#  Python QA Automation Engine

![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.12+-3776AB?style=for-the-badge&logo=python&logoColor=white)
![Playwright](https://img.shields.io/badge/Playwright-Automation-2EAD33?style=for-the-badge&logo=playwright&logoColor=white)
![pytest](https://img.shields.io/badge/pytest-Framework-0A9EDC?style=for-the-badge&logo=pytest&logoColor=white)
![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/Status-Active%20Development-brightgreen?style=for-the-badge)

An end-to-end automated UI testing framework built with **Python**, **Playwright**, and **pytest**. This project automates core user workflows and critical monetary paths for e-commerce platforms using [SauceDemo](https://www.saucedemo.com/) as the target application under test (AUT).

---

##  Project Overview

In e-commerce engineering, checkout failures directly translate to lost revenue and reduced customer trust. The **Python QA Automation Engine** provides reliable, fast, and repeatable automated test execution across multiple browser engines to catch UI regressions early in the development lifecycle.

Designed and developed with software engineering best practices, this framework demonstrates:
* **UI Automation & Verification:** Interacting with complex DOM elements and asserting UI state changes.
* **Resilient Element Selection:** Leveraging robust `data-test` attributes and explicit Playwright assertions to prevent test flakiness.
* **Modular Test Structure:** Clean file organization separating authentication workflows from core business logic.
* **Continuous Testing Readiness:** Native support for both headless (CI/CD optimized) and headed (debugging) execution modes.

---

##  Tech Stack & Dependencies

| Tool / Library | Role / Purpose |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Python 3.12+** | Core programming language |
| **Playwright (`sync_api`)** | High-performance browser automation engine (Chromium, Firefox, WebKit) |
| **pytest** | Test runner, assertions, and test execution management |
| **pytest-playwright** | Official plugin integrating Playwright fixtures into pytest |
| **Virtualenv (`venv`)** | Isolated Python runtime environment |

